.TH QSORT 3
.SH NAME
qsort \- quicker sort
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <stdlib.h>
.PP
.B void qsort(void *base, size_t nel, size_t width,
.B "        int (*compar)(const void *, const void *));"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Qsort
is an implementation
of the quicker-sort algorithm.
The first argument is a pointer to the base of the data;
the second is the number of elements;
the third is the width of an element
in bytes;
the last is the name of the comparison routine
to be called with two arguments which are pointers
to the elements being compared.
The routine must return
an integer less than, equal to, or greater than 0
according as the first argument is to be considered
less than, equal to, or greater than the second.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
sort(1), string(3)
.SH BESM-6 NOTES
.SS The width is in bytes, and a word is six of them
So sorting an array of
.B int
means
.BR "width = sizeof(int) = 6" ,
not 2 and not 4.  A page that says otherwise is quoting a different machine.
.SS The pointer comparisons are safe, and that is not luck
.I Qsort
compares partition cursors
.RB ( "i < lp" ", " "j > hp" )
and takes a difference
.RB ( "l \- a" ),
and a fat
.B char *
does
.I not
sort as a plain word: incrementing one
.B decreases
its 3-bit byte offset, which sits above the word address.
.PP
.B The compiler knows.
It lowers a relational between two fat pointers through
.BR b$pdiff ,
the same helper as
.BR \- ,
and tests the sign.  So this file is v7's arithmetic, unchanged.  See
.IR getpass (3)
for the case where the same operator
.I does
give the wrong answer, and why.
.SS The exchanges go a word at a time when they can
This is the one thing this file adds to v7, and the alignment test is expressible
in C: casting a
.B char *
to an
.B "int *"
discards the byte offset, and casting back rebuilds it as byte #0, so
.B the round trip is the identity exactly for a pointer that was already at
.B byte #0.
Two such pointers and a width that is a whole number of words mean the swap can
move words.
.SS The comparison lives in a file-scope static, as v7 has it
That is worth recording because for a time it could not.  A toolchain defect made
a call through a file-scope function pointer fail, and the routine had to carry
its comparison through a parameter instead.  It is fixed upstream, and the
structural change it forced is gone.
.PP
The durable fact underneath: a call through a function pointer is a
.B wtc
of the pointer and a bare
.BR "13 vjm" ,
wherever the pointer lives \- a parameter, an auto, an array element or a
file-scope variable.
.B wtc
carries a 15-bit address, so it reaches a global with no address escape, and a
callback needs no special handling at all.
.SH FILES
share/besm6/lib/libc.a
.br
lib/libc/gen/qsort.c
